Package: RJMCMCNucleosomes
Version: 1.37.0
Date: 2025-07-28
Title: Bayesian hierarchical model for genome-wide nucleosome
    positioning with high-throughput short-read data (MNase-Seq)
Description: This package detects nucleosome positions genome-wide from 
    paired-end or single-end MNase-Seq reads using a Bayesian hierarchical 
    model. Read positions are modelled as a mixture of Student's 
    t-distributions with an informative Multinomial-Dirichlet prior on 
    nucleosome locations, and the number of nucleosomes is estimated with a 
    reversible jump Markov chain Monte Carlo (RJMCMC) algorithm. Functions are 
    provided to split chromosomes into segments for parallel analysis, merge 
    and post-process the predictions, and plot nucleosome positions 
    alongside read coverage. This package implements the method describes in 
    Samb et al. 2015 (DOI:10.1515/sagmb-2014-0098).
